  "explanation": "10 role-complete bundles (baseline included) x 9 frozen oracle cases x 2 repeats: 180 calls, 0 retries. Bundle b_cca is the top-ranked semantically accepted set: 54/54 role cells, 18/18 threshold-0 verdicts, 9/9 stable cases, zero regressions against the baseline. Confidence is diagnostic only; production review keeps the 0.6 threshold. Anchor-tuning rationale: append-only re-evaluation after the owner-approved clarity fix that versioned ADR-SAG-0004 to v3 ('must' -> 'may'; sc-llm-provider placed in the decision-backends layer beneath sc-decision-llm). The fix does not change the prohibition's meaning, so every expected answer in the frozen v2 oracle (8b975a43...) remains correct under v3; the oracle's authority_citations still quote the v2 text because the oracle is byte-frozen. A first attempt with an extended oracle (two added sc-llm-provider probes: sc-decision-llm onto sc-llm-provider, expected satisfied; sc-agent-http onto sc-llm-provider, expected contradicted) was refused by the runner with TOURNAMENT.ORACLE_CHANGED before any Jev call; it is kept as oracle.extended-refused.json and was not worked around, so sc-llm-provider placement is not exercised by this evidence. Candidates are the nine v2 bundles unchanged plus the v2-sealed set as baseline. All ten bundles were semantically accepted (54/54, 9/9 stable, zero regressions); b_cca ranked first on reference-threshold confidence (51/54 cells at or above 0.8) and supersedes the v2-sealed b_aba (rank 3, 49/54). Production-threshold caution: on exception-claimed-1 the selected set's contradicted cell answered yes at 0.72 and 0.56; the second repeat falls below the 0.6 production threshold and would be inconclusive (underspecified) in production review. Every bundle shows low confidence on this probe (minimum 0.37 to 0.62), so it is a known weak spot of the 'temporary exception' framing, not a defect specific to b_cca. No case was relabelled, no score or selection was changed, and the active plan was not used as calibration truth.",
